      "description": "Site map of Herstmonceux Castle and surrounding area. Science buildings (red) associated with the former Royal Greenwich Observatory: 1– West Building (engineering workshop, chronometer workshop, Time Department, HM Nautical Almanac Office); 2– site maintenance workshops; 3– Solar Dome ('Nerc BGS Space Geodesy Facility'); 4– Meridian Group ('Spencer Jones Group') of instruments for positional astronomy and time determination; 5– Equatorial Group: Dome A (30-inch Thompson reflecting telescope), Dome B (36-inch Yapp reflecting telescope), Dome C (34-inch Hewitt camera), Dome D (13-inch astrographic refractor), Dome E (26-inch Thompson refractor), Dome F (38-inch Schmidt telescope); 6– West Corridor; 7– East Corridor; 8– Meteorological Enclosure; 9– Isaac Newton Telescope Dome. Other buildings (black): 10– Herstmonceux Castle; 11– parish church of All Saints. Waters (blue).",
